            "description": "Watch Qarabag vs CSKA Sofia highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 23, 2026. On July 23, 2026, Qarabag and CSKA Sofia faced off in a highly anticipated UEFA Europa League fixture. Both sides took to the pitch with high energy, looking to establish dominance in a match that promised to be a grueling test of endurance. Defensive Grime in the Opening Half The first half was a showcase of tactical discipline as both teams prioritized defensive structure over expansive attacking play. The midfield became a battleground, leading to several physical exchanges. In the 35th minute, Leandro Godoy of CSKA Sofia received the first yellow card of the match for a mistimed challenge. The tension escalated quickly when Qarabag 's Marko Jankovic was also cautioned just two minutes later. Despite the competitive spirit, neither side managed to create a clear-cut chance before the referee blew for halftime after two minutes of stoppage time. Tactical Adjustments and Late Drama The second half saw a series of strategic substitutions as both managers aimed to break the deadlock. Qarabag introduced Elvin Jafarquliyev and Renaldo Cephas early in the half to inject pace, while CSKA Sofia turned to Joel Zwarts and Isaac Solet to provide fresh legs in the 73rd minute. As the game entered its final stages, the physicality remained high, earning Facundo Rodriguez a yellow card in the 77th minute. Despite a flurry of late substitutions, including the introduction of Mohamed Brahimi for the visitors in the 91st minute, the defenses held firm through seven minutes of injury time to ensure the spoils were shared."
